# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model chain. Tried top to bottom until one answers; a tier is skipped
# entirely when its key is absent, so one key on its own is a valid setup.
#
# Capture makes many small model calls — every capture sorts, every thread
# update re-summarises, every edit is proofread — so the fastest free tiers
# come first. If every tier fails, the app still keeps the capture — saved
# verbatim and flagged unsorted, to be sorted later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Groq. https://console.groq.com/keys — very fast, generous free tier.
#    Daily free tokens reset on their own; a spent day just falls through
#    to the next tier.
# Uncomment one and paste your key after the =, or add your own line
# below — a blank GROQ_API_KEY= left in place wins over a key added later,
# because the first value for a name is the one that counts.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# 2. Cerebras. https://cloud.cerebras.ai — fast fallback when the account has
#    model access. Test the key directly before relying on it in production.
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_MODEL=gpt-oss-120b

# 3. Mistral. https://console.mistral.ai — useful fast fallback once a key is
#    configured. Accounts and model access can vary, so test the key directly
#    before relying on it in production.
#    Rate limits can be strict (429 + Retry-After when hit) —
#    the app's fail-fast chain just falls through to Gemini meanwhile.
#    mistral-small-latest is the fast workhorse; swap MISTRAL_MODEL if a
#    better fit shows up.
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-small-latest

# 4. Google AI Studio. https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — a plain AIza...
#    string. Not an OAuth client id/secret: those sign users into Google
#    accounts and cannot authenticate Gemini calls. Reliable free tier;
#    kept as the quality fallback behind the fast tiers.
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# 5. OpenRouter. https://openrouter.ai/keys — last by default. Set
#    CAPTURE_MODEL_PROVIDER=openrouter to use it first while retaining other
#    configured providers as fallbacks. A funded account still needs the exact
#    paid model slug from https://openrouter.ai/models; Capture cannot infer it.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=provider/model
# CAPTURE_MODEL_PROVIDER=openrouter
# Experimental Jev Decisions shadow. Off unless set to exactly 1. It observes
# thread/new-thread agreement after a successful sort, never changes filing,
# and requires ZDR + no-data-collection routing. Before enabling it for private
# notes, exclude this key from OpenRouter Input & Output Logging. See
# research/jev-openrouter-integration.md.
# CAPTURE_JEV_THREAD_RERANK_SHADOW=0
# Separate /api/judge observation. Also off unless set to exactly 1. It runs
# after the existing generative judge has returned all verdicts and reasons;
# it never filters candidates or replaces that call. No production prefilter
# exists until a checked-in benchmark supports an approved false-rejection
# bound. See research/jev-judge-calibration.md.
# CAPTURE_JEV_JUDGE_SHADOW=0
# Separate /api/recall observation. Also off unless set to exactly 1. It runs
# only after the existing cited answer and never reorders sources or skips that
# prose call. Structured source fields are omitted, but the bounded question
# and excerpts are not redacted. Before enabling it for private notes, exclude
# this key from Input & Output Logging, approve the additional recipient, and
# collect representative labeled evidence against an approved false-negative
# bound; synthetic results are non-promotional. See
# research/jev-recall-calibration.md.
# CAPTURE_JEV_RECALL_SHADOW=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-user password gate. Leave unset and the gate is off, which is fine
# locally. Set it in production — an open /api/sort spends someone's quota.
# The login endpoint rate-limits by client address and the model endpoints by
# address too. Both read the caller's real IP from cf-connecting-ip /
# x-real-ip / the rightmost x-forwarded-for entry. On a bare Node host with
# no proxy in front, an attacker can forge that header, so put nginx or
# Cloudflare in front before relying on the limits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limits — deployment protections, not user throttles. The real quota
# owner is the model provider, so a local single-user install needs none of
# these; set any to 0 to turn it off. Leave them at the defaults when
# hosting where strangers could reach the instance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAPTURE_MODEL_LIMIT=40        # model calls per client per minute
# CAPTURE_TTS_LIMIT=120         # speech-synthesis requests per minute
# CAPTURE_SYNC_LIMIT=60         # hub pulls/pushes per client per minute
# CAPTURE_LOGIN_LIMIT=5         # login attempts per client per 15 min

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: the human-sounding voice.
#
# Spoken replies in Distill try three engines in order: Kokoro (TTS_URL,
# near-human, runs on your Mac), then the Microsoft Edge neural voice
# (keyless, server-side, human-sounding), then the browser's built-in voice
# as the last resort. Set TTS_URL to a running Kokoro server (see SETUP.md)
# and the app switches to it automatically. Leave it unset and replies use
# the Edge neural voice — still human-sounding, and it works everywhere.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TTS_URL=http://localhost:8880/v1
# TTS_VOICE=af_bella
# EDGE_TTS_VOICE=en-US-AriaNeural

# --- Bug reports -----------------------------------------------------
# Optional. With it set, the in-app bug form files a GitHub issue directly;
# without it the form falls back to opening GitHub pre-filled, which needs
# the person to have an account.
#
# Make a FINE-GRAINED token, scoped to this one repository, with
# "Issues: Read and write" and nothing else. If it ever leaks, the worst
# anyone can do with it is open issues.
#   github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# GITHUB_ISSUE_TOKEN=
# CAPTURE_ISSUE_REPO=glebbogachev00/capture

# --- Playground (public demo instance) --------------------------------
# Build-time flag. Set ONLY on a separate Vercel project with NO
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN and NO APP_PASSWORD. It turns off sync, dictation,
# voice and the bug-report token path, and the server refuses those routes.
# Without it the app would merge every visitor's board into one hub.
#
# On that project also set tighter model limits (per IP, per minute):
#   CAPTURE_MODEL_LIMIT=8
# and a daily spend cap on the provider key itself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAYGROUND=1

# --- Capture Cloud (optional, disabled by default) ---------------------
# Cloud stores one private board for each signed-in Supabase user.
# Local Capture works when CAPTURE_CLOUD is not 1.
# Apply all files in supabase/migrations before you enable Cloud.
# Keep the Supabase secret key on the server. Never use it in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
# CAPTURE_CLOUD=1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_your-key
#
# Cloud requires a subscription by default. Set 0 only for private tests.
# CAPTURE_CLOUD_REQUIRE_SUBSCRIPTION=0
#
# --- Polar billing for Capture Cloud ----------------------------------
# Use sandbox credentials until all billing-state tests pass.
# The webhook secret comes from the registered Polar webhook endpoint.
# POLAR_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# POLAR_PRODUCT_ID_MONTHLY=
# POLAR_PRODUCT_ID_YEARLY=
# Conservative checkout/portal capability block. Do not shorten until the
# exact hosted Polar lifetime/invalidation contract is documented and tested.
# CAPTURE_POLAR_CAPABILITY_MAX_SECONDS=604800
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://trycapture.app
#
# --- Capture Cloud account erasure (internal; default off) -------------
# Do not set these from source review alone. Enable only after the exact hosted
# OTP claims, provider scopes/errors, Storage inventory/quiescence, Auth
# readback, grants/RLS/triggers, and approved Settings/legal copy are verified.
# CAPTURE_ACCOUNT_ERASURE_ENABLED=1
# CAPTURE_ACCOUNT_ERASURE_HOSTED_READY=1
# CAPTURE_ERASURE_STORAGE_INVENTORY_ATTESTED=1
# CAPTURE_ACCOUNT_ERASURE_WORKER_SECRET=<distinct random bearer, at least 32 chars>
# CAPTURE_ERASURE_AUTH_WINDOW_SECONDS=600
#
# --- Source-disabled operational maintenance ---------------------------
# Keep off until the migration, scheduler, and alert readbacks in
# docs/cloud-operational-privacy-retention.md have passed. The destination is
# an operator-owned monitor marker; the cron endpoint returns non-2xx on any
# critical aggregate and never sends identifiers/content.
# CAPTURE_OPERATIONS_ENABLED=0
# CAPTURE_OPERATIONS_WORKER_SECRET=
# CAPTURE_OPERATIONS_SCHEDULE_ID=capture-maintenance-hourly
# CAPTURE_OPERATIONS_ALERT_DESTINATION=https://alerts.example.invalid/capture
# CAPTURE_OPERATIONS_ALERTS_VERIFIED=0

# --- Sync hub: the board on Redis -------------------------------------
# Provisioned by the Vercel marketplace integration (Upstash for Redis);
# these names are injected automatically and pulled with `vercel env pull`.
# With them set, the board lives in Redis and Blob holds only pictures —
# the polling that got the Blob store suspended never touches Blob again.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
